07"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the Ras family of small GTPases. These membrane-associated proteins function as signal transducers in multiple processes including cell growth and differentiation, and dysregulation of Ras signaling has been associated with many types of cancer. The encoded protein may play a role in the tumor necrosis factor-alpha and MAP kinase signaling pathways. Alternatively spliced transcript variants encoding multiple isoforms have been observed for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Nov 2011].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"O14807","text":"Signal transducer in the Ras-MAPK signaling pathway that regulates cell proliferation and survival (PubMed:16630891, PubMed:28289718, PubMed:35768504, PubMed:35830882, PubMed:35831509, PubMed:36175670). Core component of the SHOC2-MRAS-PP1c (SMP) holophosphatase complex that regulates the MAPK pathway activation (PubMed:16630891, PubMed:35768504, PubMed:35830882, PubMed:35831509, PubMed:36175670). The formation of the SMP complex only occurs when MRAS is GTP-bound (PubMed:35768504, PubMed:35830882, PubMed:35831509, PubMed:36175670, PubMed:39809765). Unlike other Ras proteins, MRAS has low intrinsic GTPase activity and may require additional factors for activation (PubMed:39809765). The SMP complex specifically dephosphorylates the inhibitory phosphorylation at 'Ser-259' of RAF1 kinase, 'Ser-365' of BRAF kinase and 'Ser-214' of ARAF kinase, stimulating their kinase activities (PubMed:16630891, PubMed:35768504, PubMed:35830882, PubMed:35831509, PubMed:36175670). Recognized by LZTR1 that mediates its ubiquitination by a BCR (BTB-CUL3-RBX1) E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase complex (PubMed:40934300)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_03","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"O14807","pdb_id":"7txh","het_id":"GNP","resolution":1.95,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Green et al. 2024"],"ligand_name":"GMP-PNP","ligand_class":"cofactor or substrate","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Human MRas Q71R in complex with human Shoc2 LRR domain M173I and human PP1Ca","first_author":"Hauseman, Z.J.","n_authors":24,"journal":"Nature","year":2022,"doi":"10.1038/s41586-022-05086-1","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-05086-1"},{"accession":"O14807","pdb_id":"9o0p","het_id":"6IC","resolution":1.5,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"SUBJECT_OF_INVESTIGATION","datasets":["Green et al. 2024"],"ligand_name":"MRTX-1133","ligand_class":"drug-like or studied compound","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Crystal structure of GDP-bound mutant MRAS in complex with MRTX1133","first_author":"Bonsor, D.A.","n_authors":12,"journal":"Nat Commun","year":2026,"doi":"10.1038/s41467-026-68319-1","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-68319-1"},{"accession":"O14807","pdb_id":"9o0q","het_id":"6IC","resolution":1.9,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"SUBJECT_OF_INVESTIGATION","datasets":["Green et al. 2024"],"ligand_name":"MRTX-1133","ligand_class":"drug-like or studied compound","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Crystal structure of GMPPNP-bound mutant MRAS in complex with MRTX1133","first_author":"Bonsor, D.A.","n_authors":12,"journal":"Nat Commun","year":2026,"doi":"10.1038/s41467-026-68319-1","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-026-68319-1"}],"alphafold_accessions":["O14807"]}